Steve,

  It depends on your local time
zone setting (options("time.zone")). You can change that, or
force data to be read in a consistent time zone like this:

timeDate("4/04/2006 0:00:00 AM",in.format="%m/%d/%Y
%H:%M:%S %p", zone='GMT')-timeDate("3/10/2006 0:00:00 AM",in.format="%m/%d/%Y
%H:%M:%S %p", zone='GMT')

Dave

"Steve Su" <ssu at thegeorgeinstitute.org>

Sent by: s-news-owner at lists.biostat.wustl.edu
04/30/2006 06:40 PM

To

<s-news at lists.biostat.wustl.edu>

cc

Subject

[S] Splus 6.0 calculating time differences
in timeDate()

Dear All,

 

Does Splus 6.0 and later account for daylight
saving automatically?

*The following is in month day year format”

 

In calculating the following I get 25 days
and 1 hour:

 

timeDate("4/04/2006 0:00:00 AM",in.format="%m/%d/%Y
%H:%M:%S %p")-timeDate("3/10/2006 0:00:00 AM",in.format="%m/%d/%Y
%H:%M:%S %p")

 

Is it possible not to have this adjustment?
Or is Splus doing something I am not aware of?

 

Thank you for your attention.

 

Steve.

