From dimitris.rizopoulos at med.kuleuven.be  Thu May  4 14:19:27 2006
From: dimitris.rizopoulos at med.kuleuven.be (Dimitris Rizopoulos)
Date: Thu, 04 May 2006 16:19:27 +0200
Subject: Re: Generate random numbers knowing median and inter-quartiles only
References: <445A0976.6000306@bangor.ac.uk>
Message-ID: <020f01c66f85$c0a4d800$0540210a@www.domain>

if you want to simulate from normal you only need median (which is 
also the mean) and one quantile since you only need to find the 
standard deviation, e.g.,

q1 <- qnorm(0.25, sd = 5.12)
######################
sigma <- function(sd, q, p, mean){
p - pnorm(q, mean, sd)
}
sd <- uniroot(sigma, c(.Machine$double.eps^0.25, 100), q = q1, p = 
0.25, mean = 0)$root

# then

x <- rnorm(100, 0, sd)

I hope it helps.

Best,
Dimitris

